cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  CAVAL: A Cost-Aware Validation System for Tradable-Alpha
  Discovery with False Discovery Rate Control
message: >-
  If you use this software or its methodology, please cite both
  the software (this record) and the associated paper.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Paritosh
    family-names: Dwivedi
    affiliation: Vellore Institute of Technology
    email: paritosh.dwivedi2024@vitstudent.ac.in
  - given-names: Ramanathan
    family-names: Lakshmanan
    affiliation: Vellore Institute of Technology
    email: lramanathan@vit.ac.in
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1532-5495'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/pdwi2020/cost-aware-alpha-paper'
abstract: >-
  CAVAL is a modular expert-system pipeline that admits an equity
  long-short signal only if it clears a data-integrity pre-screen
  (Screen 0) and four sequential validation screens: Benjamini-Hochberg
  false-discovery-rate control, a permutation-calibrated Tradable-Alpha
  FDR test, an Alpha Robustness Volume cost-robustness metric, and a
  single-touch locked out-of-sample evaluation with PBO/CSCV and
  Deflated-Sharpe-Ratio guards and conformal calibration.
keywords:
  - algorithmic trading
  - false discovery rate
  - market impact
  - backtest overfitting
  - conformal prediction
  - walk-forward validation
license: MIT
